Queueable — the modern async default
apex
public class ErpSyncJob implements Queueable {
    public void execute(QueueableContext ctx) { ... }
}

Id jobId = System.enqueueJob(new ErpSyncJob(accounts));

One method, one interface. The interesting part is everything @future couldn't do.

***************************************************************************************************************************************************************

Advantages over @future
	                                                                           @future	                                                                                                          Queueable
Parameters	                                                     Primitives + collections of primitives	                                                                Any type — sObjects, custom classes, Maps of objects
Return	                                                                     void, no handle	                                                                                  Job ID (AsyncApexJob) for monitoring
Chaining	                                                                     Impossible	                                                                                Yes — one child per parent, unlimited depth in production
Callable from                                                             	Trigger, sync Apex	                                                                          Trigger, sync Apex, Queueable, Batch finish(), Schedulable
