2. Monitoring
apex
Id jobId = System.enqueueJob(new ErpSyncJob(accts));

AsyncApexJob job = [
    SELECT Id, Status, NumberOfErrors, ExtendedStatus, CompletedDate
    FROM AsyncApexJob WHERE Id = :jobId
];

Status moves through Queued → Processing → Completed | Failed | Aborted. You can surface progress to a user in LWC, store the ID on a record, or abort with System.abortJob(jobId). @future gives you none of this — a silent failure stays silent.

